inline.s:
Fine trees stand all around, their shadows spread and sparse;
beneath the trees a little cottage lies well hid.
No carriage or horse is heard, all human tracks cut off;
the gate shut, all day long I sit cross-legged alone.

For thirty years and more I have studied laziness and ease;
my whole life sits cut off on Mount Zhurong.
This crane-boned body is light — speak no more of age;
a thousand feet below, look at the pine my own hand planted.

Grown old in the blue hills, I bear my lord's grace;
south of Mount Kuang I lie facing the morning sun.
The Seven Worthies and Five Elders face each other from afar;
the spring's sound speaks deeply of the gate of non-duality.
